# Neurophysiological rationale:
# Clinical ECG interpretation follows a systematic approach:
# 1. Rate assessment (brady/normo/tachycardia)
# 2. Rhythm classification (sinus, atrial, ventricular)
# 3. Morphological analysis (axis, intervals, segments)
# 4. Diagnostic correlation with coding systems
# Automated systems must present findings in clinical terminology while
# maintaining appropriate disclaimers about algorithmic limitations.
# (Rautaharju et al., 2009 - AHA/ACCF/HRS recommendations)

